<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for Tiegel.app, signed with the Hardened Runtime
  (codesign option "runtime"). Intentionally empty:

  * No App Sandbox: Tiegel starts php, docker, git and language servers from
    the user's PATH and edits arbitrary project folders. The sandbox would
    forbid both.

  * No com.apple.security.network.server / .network.client: these are App
    Sandbox entitlements and have no effect on non-sandboxed apps. The local
    DBGp listener (port 9003) and the opt-in update check work without them.
    (Listening on a non-loopback address may trigger the macOS application
    firewall prompt; that is a user setting, not an entitlement.)

  * No com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory /
    disable-library-validation: the Go runtime and cgo code (Gio/Metal,
    Tree-sitter) are fully ahead-of-time compiled and need none of these
    Hardened Runtime exceptions. Child processes (php, docker, git) are
    separate executables and are not restricted by Tiegel's runtime flags.

  Add exceptions here only with a documented reason (docs/DECISIONS.md).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
